Business Plan/files/Night Tasks/logs/

# ── Untracked credential notes (NEVER commit) ─────────────────────
# These sit in Business Plan/files/ and hold real values, including
# META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKENS. They were never tracked -- these rules exist so a
# stray `git add -A` cannot make them public, which is exactly how
# stripe_backup_code.txt ended up readable for 103 days.
Business Plan/files/Environment Variables.txt
*Environment Variables*
*Set env vars*
*env_vars*
# ── Stripe 2FA recovery material ──────────────────────────────────
# This file sat in a PUBLIC repo from 2026-05-09 to 2026-08-21 (103 days).
# It is a two-step-authentication BACKUP CODE, not an API key -- rotating
# API keys does nothing about it; the codes must be regenerated in
# Dashboard -> Settings -> Your account -> Two-step authentication.
# Untracked rather than deleted so the local copy survives until then.
# NOTE: untracking does NOT remove it from git history.
Business Plan/files/stripe_backup_code.txt
*backup_code*

# ── content/ is a two-file directory, on purpose ──────────────────
# queue.csv and brand.json are the source of truth for the social calendar.
# Nothing else belongs here. Design source masters (31.5 MB of PNG) and the
# superseded worksheets were once pasted in, which would have put binaries
# git can never forget into a public repo -- and undone the point of moving
# the queue out of a folder full of near-identical copies.
#
# Deny-by-default so an accidental paste cannot be committed. To add a
# genuinely new file here, add a matching `!` line below.
content/*
!content/queue.csv
!content/brand.json

# Source art and superseded exports live in OneDrive, not the repo:
#   OneDrive\SparkDate\SourceArt              <- the PNG masters
#   OneDrive\SparkDate\Superseded_2026-08-22  <- the dead worksheets
# Published JPEGs are committed at public/social/ -- those are the ones that
# actually publish, and they are ~2.5 MB rather than 31.5 MB.
*_SUPERSEDED_*/
